DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The uuccoomm driver attaches to USB modems, serial ports, and other devices
     that need to look like a tty.  The uuccoomm driver behaves like a tty(4):
     this means that normal programs such as cu(1) or pppd(8) can be used to
     access the device.

     The _p_o_r_t_n_o locator can be used to decide which port to use for devices
     that have multiple external ports.

FFIILLEESS
     /dev/ttyU?    tty devices
     /dev/cuaU?    call out devices (see tty(4))

